      "Security work is text work: logs, JSON, HTTP responses. Python's model fits perfectly — open a file, iterate lines, test with 'in', extract fields with split() or the re module, accumulate counts in a dict, print a sorted report. The example below is complete and runnable: it counts failed logins per IP from an auth log, the Python twin of the Level 3 bash pipeline — same logic, more structure, easier to extend (thresholds, JSON output, unit tests).",
